WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.460
The Evil Witch Doctor has set lots of traps for you before you can face him one on one.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:08.100
Are you up for the challenge?

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.920
Can you live through Adventure Island to save Princess Leilani?

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:35.680
And welcome to NEStalgia, chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:39.020
I'm Mike. I'm Joe.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:41.340
And who do we have up?

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:42.200
I'm Sean.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.260
All right, we got Sean and Joe in the house.

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:46.440
All right. Some might consider that a full house,

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:50.900
but usually you need Uncle Jesse and Bob Saget on the show too to make it a full house.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:52.940
You don't remember his name, do you?

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:54.500
Well, I don't remember his name on the show.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:55.480
Danny. Danny Tamarillo. Danny Tanner.

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:57.240
Danny Tamarillo is all that.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.040
He's all that. That's funny.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:00.140
But you know what?

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:05.580
Even if I can't remember names, people remember us and sometimes they write to us on the show.

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:09.500
Wow. And we did get a write-in from Steven.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:11.240
Okay. What's up, Steven?

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:15.660
Yeah. Steven wrote in, Dear Sweet Baby Boys of Nostalgia.

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.020
I love it.

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:22.380
All right? He said he's been working through our back catalog and savoring it like fine wine.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.140
He's currently on the RC Pro-Am episode, hopefully a little later into the show by now.

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:32.060
He said that he would like to know what is the best Capcom box art.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:34.340
And he even attached some images, for example.

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:38.180
But we should keep it to just the ones that we've played so far.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:44.080
And with that in mind, I'm going to automatically disqualify Mega Man from being the best.

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:44.940
That's not fair.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:46.240
That's not fair, Mike.

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:50.280
Why isn't that fair? It's favorite, not best, right?

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:52.280
I don't even get any joy looking at this.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.200
I feel so much joy when I look at that.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:56.220
I still wonder what's even going on.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:02.020
I don't even remember anything from any of the levels that represent that part of the box art.

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:04.320
So you don't watch bad movies for the fun of it?

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:08.120
Yeah, you can like it ironically or even just because it's funny looking.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:12.400
Yeah. Yeah. Okay. I'm conceding the point a little bit, but I still don't think...

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:15.220
It is definitively not enjoyable.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:19.620
For me, box art is all about like, if that's what you're picking...

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:20.600
It's like a record cover.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:30.640
If you're going to pick to listen to or to play something based off of just the box art alone, Mega Man doesn't really sell me that that's an awesome game, which is currently on our essential games list.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:33.400
Well, it's like the old adage goes, judge a book by its cover.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:34.240
Yeah, that's true.

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:37.320
Exactly. And that's exactly how everybody did it at Blockbuster, right?

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:38.680
Like that's how... 100%.

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:45.660
That was my thought process on things was like, you know, maybe if it came down to it, I'd read the back of the box also to like...

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:48.240
I like you every day read the back of the box.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:49.520
Very good. Every Friday.

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:52.080
That's how I... Well, it's every day that we record these.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:54.400
Yeah, we've been recording every day for three years.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:03:01.540
Yeah. Gun Smoke is the one that I think is the best because it captures that whole...

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:09.040
Like it's a cool cover first off, but then it also captures the vibe of like a Western and has like a cool like spaghetti Western thing going on.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:13.880
And I just think like that for me is the best, is the closest.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:22.660
Is this maybe something like 1942 like actually just straight up tells you this is a World War II shooter flyer game?

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:24.920
Like maybe that's good too?

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:30.200
What do you guys think? Well, going on the idea of like when I was a kid, what would have drawn me in?

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:31.540
Gun Smoke is a good one.

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:33.660
I also really like Section Z.

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:35.600
Oh, yeah. Section Z is cool.

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:36.440
I think there's a badass on there.

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:39.340
This little like guy in a Iron Man looking suit.

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:41.620
I think I would have been drawn to that.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:45.380
Yeah. And also like it looks like the rest of the backdrop is just black.

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:50.600
But if you look carefully, there is like a lot of detail of other ships and stuff going on in there.

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:52.060
So, yeah, I'm a fan of that one.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:57.680
Sean? Well, since you've disqualified the one that I actually enjoy the most,

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:04.440
and since Gun Smoke is probably the best looking, I'm going to just have to go with, you know, just another tidbit.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:10.100
Like, you know, I like the Ghosts and Goblins one because it looks like a really bad family photo.

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:17.960
And the rest of the box arts are just sort of bland to me.

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:21.740
At least this one just looks like Monsters, Inc.

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:24.280
Is the main character like posing with the Ghosts and Goblins?

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:26.160
Yeah. They're all like, oh, let's get in for a group photo.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:36.420
Yeah, and then one that I also have to call out is the Commando one because it says destroy the enemy army over it in just like aerial text.

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:39.200
You know, like yellow aerial text.

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:41.080
Destroy the enemy army.

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:43.040
Like that's how it's written out.

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:46.140
Nice. So we're not going to talk about Capcom today, though.

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:48.460
We are talking about Adventure Island.

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:51.140
Have you guys ever heard that name before?

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:52.800
I knew of it before this.

00:04:52.820 --> 00:04:56.080
I had never played it, but I think I've even seen like some screenshots of it before.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:59.600
Got it. It sort of sounds like a generic like template game.

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:02.080
So that's what I had to expect.

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:05.920
It's the name of like every theme park in every state, right?

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:08.540
Like every state needs to have an Adventure Island.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:11.640
Yeah. So yeah, I knew of the franchise.

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:17.080
Like I had heard of that there was like many of these different types of games, but I never played any of them.

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:18.720
So I was excited to get into it.

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:27.020
Basically, it's a Super Mario Brothers knockoff in many ways, which is funny because in the last episode, Sean and I had discussed, Joe, you weren't on it.

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:34.480
I wasn't. We had discussed that one of the things I was looking forward to is somebody just taking the Super Mario Brothers formula and just trying to get like close to it.

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:35.960
Like not do something so stupid.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:40.460
We were referring to Karnov and being like, why did they have to add all those extra things?

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:42.220
Like just you didn't even get the jump right.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:43.360
At least focus on that.

00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:48.580
And so I get huge Super Mario Brothers vibes out of Adventure Island.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:52.780
What about you two? Particularly because of the way it controls, I get those vibes.

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:57.960
I mean, it's also like it seems like it should be a given, but it's not when it comes to platformers.

00:05:58.060 --> 00:06:02.520
It's also just like well-designed and enemy placement and platforming.

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:11.060
But just the fact that you have, I think we said it about Mario, your character has like weight and momentum and that makes it feel to me so much better to control.

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:14.880
And that's where I got the most like, wow, this reminds me of Super Mario.

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:21.720
I agree. It has tastes of Super Mario in it and that's all I'll say on it for now.

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:30.800
Cool. Just to give an overview of the game, Caveman Mario has to survive eight worlds, four stages in each.

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:37.700
Each, running and jumping his way through each stage and at the last stage of each world, there's a boss.

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:42.220
So emphasis on Caveman Mario because that's pretty much Super Mario Brothers.

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:46.020
There's the same amount of number of levels as Super Mario Brothers.

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:47.920
Now, why did you say Caveman Mario?

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:53.940
Because I think that this is just, you know, based on the way that this game plays.

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:58.040
It's like taking Mario and putting him in the Flintstones.

00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:00.620
It sounds like you were like actually reading something.

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:02.700
No, I wasn't reading anything.

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:13.520
I said that. I think actually there's a backstory to the main character's name because he's based off of a Hudson Soft employee, Takahashi Majin.

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:21.820
And this guy is something of a legend in Japan because he was known as 16-shot.

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:24.160
Why do you think they called him 16-shot?

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:28.820
I imagine he has a loaded gun in the office at all times.

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:31.100
That's a good idea for an employee to have.

00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:39.320
No, it's because he was able and documented to hit the A button on an NES controller 16 times in a second.

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:42.120
Wow. 16 times in a second.

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:43.480
He's like a human turbo button.

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:45.180
Yeah, I think that's pretty impressive.

00:07:45.180 --> 00:07:47.120
I don't know what I was hitting per second.

00:07:47.140 --> 00:07:49.480
I would like to know how long he can sustain that, though.

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:53.500
Well, he did an injury much later on in like his 50s, and he said he'd be better.

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:55.700
He'd be closer to like 13-shot by now.

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:56.940
Oof. He doesn't think.

00:07:57.220 --> 00:07:59.180
16 is kind of unheard of.

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:01.560
Like, as far as I know.

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:03.740
Do people record this?

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:05.160
None of the guests. Well, there's a game.

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:12.760
There's like, just to go on a tangent for a second, there's a mini game in Mario Party, like, 4 or 5, where even, it's called Domination.

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:15.720
This is how we figured it out.

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:19.680
Yeah, and the whole time you just hit the A button for 10 seconds, right?

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:26.480
And then I figured eventually, once I was scoring like in the 100 pluses, I was like, oh, how many, like, is that per second?

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:28.280
And then I'd be like, oh, you just divide by 10.

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:30.180
So, I think I did.

00:08:30.180 --> 00:08:31.520
You're taking us through like the way you learned.

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:38.180
Yeah, so I got to like 100 and maybe like 11 at one point, and that's 11 A presses per second.

00:08:38.740 --> 00:08:39.780
That's more than 11.

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:41.480
11.1, yes.

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:42.500
You can go ahead and round that up.

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:44.060
I don't care about it at .5.

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:45.240
You can round up at .1.

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:47.000
Just to one other decimal.

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:48.820
And that's not even close to 16, though.

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:53.540
Like, if I'm getting 111 in 10 seconds, that means that Takehashi would get 160.

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:55.480
Astounding. This is astounding.

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:56.860
Yeah. You know what's funny, though?

00:08:56.960 --> 00:09:04.000
It has nothing to do with Adventure Island because you wouldn't gain any benefits from having like turbo-like features in Adventure Island.

00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:14.980
Another quick fact before we get into the game is that Hudson Soft made this game, but it is a direct port pretty much of the Sega arcade game Wonder Boy.

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:16.600
I love it.

00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:27.560
Which is just weird because, you know, like, Hudson Soft attained the partial rights to Wonder Boy, but Wonder Boy wound up being sold to Sega at the same time.

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:32.440
And so they weren't allowed to use the name Wonder Boy, but they owned the rights to use the game.

00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:35.780
Wow. So they just figured, oh, we'll just call it something different.

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:39.340
And that's how they came up with Adventure Island on the NES.

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:42.460
It does suck. Wonder Boy's a great name.

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:47.060
You can play Wonder Boy on, I believe, the Sega Master System and probably even the Sega Genesis.

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:50.980
But I just think that's funny because Wonder Boy is still around.

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:52.360
I don't think Adventure Island is.

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:16.060
And now it's time to talk about Adventure Island itself.

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:20.140
Joe, you mentioned that there's this whole weight and momentum thing.

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:26.600
I think it's really important, since we've emphasized so many times about the jump in platformers, that we really get nitty-gritty on this.

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:29.640
So, Joe, if you could just kind of start the conversation and we'll go from there.

00:10:29.780 --> 00:10:37.520
Yeah. So, I mean, by weight, I just mean that as you move, when you take your finger off of the direction you're moving, you kind of slide a little bit or you keep running a little bit.

00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:41.500
And as much as when you say that out loud, it sounds like, oh, that sucks.

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:48.120
But really, in practice, it feels to me, maybe it's because we're conditioned by games like Mario, it feels much more natural.

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:59.840
Yeah. And it feels like you can use that to time your jumps a little better, which also leads to the fact that there are two jumps in this game.

00:10:59.980 --> 00:11:03.460
There's your regular jump if you're standing still, where you jump kind of low.

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:06.400
And then if you're running and jumping, you jump pretty high.

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:10.840
Or you can just press both buttons at the same time if you want to cheat it.

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:17.400
But that felt kind of, it took a little getting used to, but it felt kind of good once you got the hang of it.

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:20.120
And how about at full speed, right?

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:21.320
Like Super Mario Bros.

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:26.120
has that arch, right, of the maximum jump that you can get.

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:37.420
And what's good about that is if you start going the other way or while you're in midair, there's a lot of flexibility so that you don't have to be so perfect about your positioning at any given time.

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:41.320
Because you can kind of back out of decisions when you see a platform arise.

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:43.280
Or you can move forward a little more.

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:46.420
Or you can stop right where you are and just fall straight down.

00:11:46.620 --> 00:11:47.720
How does that feel here?

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:55.520
To be honest, I'm not, I can't think of how exactly it works, which makes me think that it works in a similar way.

00:11:55.620 --> 00:11:57.240
I think it felt heavier.

00:11:57.440 --> 00:11:59.900
Like it's harder to get to your max speed.

00:12:00.220 --> 00:12:09.960
It's harder to, you definitely can adjust in midair, but it feels like there's much more resisting you when you do that.

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:16.920
But all in all, it feels like the same technique with the numbers tweaked.

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:22.260
Yeah, and I think actually the weight thing comes from a graphics thing, actually.

00:12:22.580 --> 00:12:28.260
The way that the graphics are designed in this game to make them look nicer than, say, Super Mario Bros.

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:29.220
did back in 85,

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:34.000
is that they've increased the size of every kind of graphic.

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:38.340
So the sprites are bigger, but now you have less on your display at a given moment.

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:44.600
And so I don't even know if, like, well, if you did just shrink everything down, would it actually get very close to Super Mario Bros.

00:12:44.600 --> 00:12:51.460
And is it just the fact that because he's bigger and because you're seeing less of the stage that it just feels more weighty on every action?

00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:55.480
You would think that it would feel faster, though, if it was actually the one-to-one.

00:12:55.760 --> 00:12:57.220
Right. That's why I think it's not.

00:12:57.620 --> 00:13:04.620
Got it. Yeah, and when you mentioned before, like, the arc that Mario has, I think his is a much wider arc,

00:13:04.660 --> 00:13:11.060
whereas this guy, whatever his name is, he has, like, a very high arch, but he falls fast, too.

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:16.640
So I think that makes it a little harder, not necessarily in a better or worse way,

00:13:16.740 --> 00:13:19.260
but just it's a little more difficult, I think, to time.

00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:21.560
Like, I want to land in between those two enemies.

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:23.100
I want to land in between those two rocks.

00:13:23.100 --> 00:13:27.940
How many times did you have this phenomena while playing the game where, like, you jump over something,

00:13:28.380 --> 00:13:34.120
and then you immediately, like, as you're coming down, you're, like, prepared to do just another jump just in case.

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:38.020
So you, like, jump over something, and then you're just ready to do the next jump already,

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:40.840
and you just, even if you just jump straight up and come right back down,

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:46.420
I just felt like I was tapping the jump button a lot because this game doesn't have the Super Mario Bros.

00:13:46.420 --> 00:13:53.100
there's a mechanic of stomping on enemies, so you can only throw your hammers at enemies to take them down,

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:57.220
which works a lot like the fireball in the Fire Flower Power Up.

00:13:58.240 --> 00:14:02.660
I guess what I'm saying is that there's a lot of jumping, emphasis on jumping on this game,

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:07.640
more so than using the hammer, but the hammer comes in handy,

00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:11.720
but because you're taught to jump more often than you're taught to throw the hammer,

00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:15.240
there was a lot of times I just found myself trying to avoid everything rather than, like,

00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:17.560
take things slow and combat the situation.

00:14:17.840 --> 00:14:27.360
Well, you're sort of incentivized to fireball or hammer things just so that you can get those eggs

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:32.940
that may or may not have something good in them, or points, which, you know, points is points,

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:35.140
but you do get extra lives that way.

00:14:36.400 --> 00:14:39.680
But I think I did like a combination of the two.

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:46.460
Like, I would avoid if I definitely knew I didn't have time to destroy it,

00:14:46.680 --> 00:14:48.520
but I think I was pretty balanced.

00:14:48.980 --> 00:14:50.400
Yeah, I kind of feel the same way.

00:14:50.500 --> 00:14:53.260
I wasn't really super heavy one way or another.

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:58.100
I was doing a lot of jumping, and I was constantly throwing axes because, I mean,

00:14:58.160 --> 00:15:01.800
I feel like I definitely had a lot of agency and, like, oh, I want to hit this guy, I want to hit that guy,

00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:06.080
but also when I wasn't aiming for things, I was just throwing axes because odds are I'm going to hit something.

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:07.900
And there's no limit to the axes, correct?

00:15:08.160 --> 00:15:13.260
No. They don't do anything in terms of that meter that acts as a timeout.

00:15:13.520 --> 00:15:15.500
Just spam them. Yeah.

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:19.900
So I actually like the idea of, like, having permanent fire flower.

00:15:20.740 --> 00:15:28.440
I thought it would be strange because that same button that you use to throw the hammers is the same button that you use to run.

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:32.740
Yeah. And that gets a little trickier later on.

00:15:32.860 --> 00:15:34.280
Oh, it's definitely tricky.

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:40.780
Yeah. Later on, it definitely has, like, more enemies appear on the screen, and the real estate of your platforms shrinks.

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:44.500
It becomes a little bit of, like, well, what does the game want me to do?

00:15:44.600 --> 00:15:49.880
Does it want me to rush through this stage as fast as I can, or does it want me to figure out, like, the best way to deal with the enemies?

00:15:49.880 --> 00:16:10.480
Because that's another huge problem with this whole balancing of the jump and the platforming is that there's that timer that acts as, like, your life at the same time that, basically, if you ever trip over a rock, you lose some of that chunk of meter that acts as your timer.

00:16:10.480 --> 00:16:17.820
Just as it goes on throughout the stage, it slowly goes away, too, and the only way to increase it is to eat a bunch of fruit.

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:20.620
Now, granted, the fruit spawns all over the place randomly.

00:16:21.180 --> 00:16:22.500
Poppin's pretty bad on this.

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:25.780
It feels like sometimes it appears while I'm, like, right next to it.

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:27.380
It's like, how did I not see it yet?

00:16:27.620 --> 00:16:31.120
I liken that to if the coins in Super Mario Bros.

00:16:31.180 --> 00:16:32.440
just popped on whenever.

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:36.140
Like, whenever you see that, as soon as you see them, they're just like, oh, cool, those are the coins.

00:16:36.260 --> 00:16:37.900
They don't just, like, show up randomly.

00:16:38.380 --> 00:16:43.040
But the fruit just is like, oh, here's a banana all the way up there, and then there's a cherry down here.

00:16:43.400 --> 00:16:46.060
I never got one in a spot where it would spawn and kill you.

00:16:46.300 --> 00:16:48.980
You know, like, you would jump into it and then fall into a pit.

00:16:49.260 --> 00:16:56.800
So they must be thinking about where these things are going to spawn, but they just didn't think about, like, oh, you have to see them to know that you should grab them.

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:59.740
Yeah, and there are some times where it's spawning.

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:04.520
It spawns so late where it's like you kind of have to plan to be running so you can jump high enough.

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:06.200
You have to kind of, like, plan ahead to get a few of them.

00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:08.700
So there's a few times where I definitely missed some because of some.

00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:11.860
Yeah, I definitely wasn't a fruit completionist.

00:17:12.020 --> 00:17:15.740
I collected them when they were convenient, but I ignored them if I didn't.

00:17:15.740 --> 00:17:25.380
I wasn't either, but as far as the way I normally play, I definitely collected a lot more than I usually would if it was just for points or something like that.

00:17:25.420 --> 00:17:26.880
Because I knew it was helping my life.

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:29.380
And there was just something satisfying about collecting them.

00:17:29.380 --> 00:17:33.420
So I was, like, trying more than I usually do to, like, collect as many as I could.

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:34.920
It's a balance of things, right?

00:17:35.020 --> 00:17:40.040
Because, you know, Joe, as you just mentioned, it incentivizes collecting them because it actually does something.

00:17:40.280 --> 00:17:48.720
But, and maybe this is just, like, my 2020 way of thinking that there just shouldn't, if there's going to be some kind of limit like that,

00:17:48.720 --> 00:17:55.140
it's just put a timer on the top right of the screen and just tell me, like, I got 200 seconds to make it through the stage.

00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:57.020
I feel like we would complain about the timer.

00:17:57.200 --> 00:17:59.020
Yeah. We would have complained about the timer regardless, right?

00:17:59.120 --> 00:18:05.980
Yeah. But I'm saying, like, to complicate it in a way where it's, like, you know, everything in this game one shot kills you except for these rocks,

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:08.660
which happen to just take away some measly meter from you.

00:18:08.720 --> 00:18:12.780
It's, like, at what point do we just say, like, screw the meter, the game's hard enough as it is.

00:18:12.880 --> 00:18:13.780
But it's not. It's not.

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:14.780
I just want to get that out of the way.

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:23.120
It's not too hard. You know, the meter just seems like an extra layer on top of an overall, like, fun, laid-back kind of game.

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:24.580
Yeah, you know, Mike. It made it stressful.

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:30.800
I think that, yeah, we should just definitely redesign all the levels so that you just have to press right until you hit the end.

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:32.560
There shouldn't be any platforming.

00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:33.760
Yeah. Or obstacles.

00:18:34.060 --> 00:18:36.460
Yeah. I don't understand how in these caves there's all these holes.

00:18:37.240 --> 00:18:39.800
You know, like, it just doesn't check out.

00:18:39.980 --> 00:18:49.180
No, I'm not crazy about the meter or a timer, but I think I actually prefer the meter just because I like the idea that you have some control in, like, building the timer back up.

00:18:49.340 --> 00:18:51.140
It feels a little less arbitrary.

00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:54.120
Yeah, exactly. It feels like I'm doing something.

00:18:54.900 --> 00:19:02.820
Yeah. If I were, if it were my option, it would just be a game where the platforming is challenging enough where you don't need that.

00:19:02.940 --> 00:19:03.980
But, I mean, that's a different game.

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:04.880
I mean, that's just my preference.

00:19:05.960 --> 00:19:13.760
Right. So, I mean, you know, there's a lot to say, though, about the relaxing element of this game with the music.

00:19:13.760 --> 00:19:18.040
It's fantastic. And it's fun to be, like, in these prehistoric times.

00:19:18.180 --> 00:19:19.300
And the only thing you're going up to get.

00:19:19.320 --> 00:19:20.960
Is it prehistoric? It's got to be, right?

00:19:21.160 --> 00:19:22.400
No, I kept thinking that, too.

00:19:22.560 --> 00:19:23.500
But is it?

00:19:23.500 --> 00:19:24.960
It definitely plays in its own universe.

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:27.080
I'm not saying it takes place for our dinosaurs.

00:19:27.080 --> 00:19:33.180
It says in the manual, you're on an island in the South Pacific, which I feel like it wouldn't say if we were in prehistoric times.

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:34.860
I don't think we're. What, because it'd have to say Pangea?

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:38.820
I don't know. I guess it's just, like, weird to specify, like, a location.

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:42.480
Mike, I think you sort of headcanoned this into the Stone Age.

00:19:42.480 --> 00:19:44.780
So forget the prehistoric thing for a second.

00:19:44.940 --> 00:19:45.800
Maybe the Flintstones are hot.

00:19:45.800 --> 00:19:47.060
He's wearing a baseball cap. Yeah.

00:19:47.520 --> 00:19:52.040
Maybe the Flintstones are hot at this moment and they just figured they'll cash in on the dinosaur aesthetic.

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:54.000
But forget about that.

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:56.840
I just think, like, the graphics are fun and silly.

00:19:57.100 --> 00:20:04.880
The only enemies you ever face are not really that scary by any means, except for the boss, which is a little bit of a weird misnomer.

00:20:05.080 --> 00:20:10.420
But there's just, like, most of this game is actually fun and enjoyable and colorful.

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:18.380
And I think there's something to be said there about the color palette of this game versus regular NES games we play.

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:20.680
I feel like most NES games we play are not that vibrant.

00:20:20.820 --> 00:20:26.200
Yeah. This is almost, like, making me think more of, like, Super Mario Bros.

00:20:26.340 --> 00:20:27.160
3 colors.

00:20:27.320 --> 00:20:28.680
Like, that's a really colorful game.

00:20:29.560 --> 00:20:37.940
And I don't think we've had anything like, well, maybe we have, but not that many things that are, like, this close to that kind of aesthetic feel.

00:20:37.940 --> 00:20:45.900
Yeah. But we should probably talk about those bosses or it's just one guy whose head just continues to change.

00:20:46.280 --> 00:20:50.780
Because is that not the most disappointing part of this entire game?

00:20:51.660 --> 00:20:53.020
It is very disappointing.

00:20:53.320 --> 00:20:59.560
I have problems with both instances of this game between the levels themselves and the bosses.

00:21:00.040 --> 00:21:04.500
Yes, the bosses are disappointing because it's the same thing every time.

00:21:04.500 --> 00:21:06.780
You just try and Dracula them.

00:21:07.380 --> 00:21:09.620
Like, jump up, hit the head, jump up, hit the head.

00:21:09.920 --> 00:21:11.440
And it's not even that many.

00:21:11.640 --> 00:21:16.960
Right. And, like, the hardest part of, like, not dying is, like...

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:18.900
Make sure you're not jumping when he throws.

00:21:19.140 --> 00:21:21.600
Right. Like, just... He has a very slow, arced thing.

00:21:21.740 --> 00:21:23.640
He's easier than some of the regular enemies that come up.

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:25.880
And then he, like, walks towards you to a certain point.

00:21:25.900 --> 00:21:28.720
So, just, like, don't be there when he's walking there.

00:21:28.740 --> 00:21:29.840
It's, like, really that simple.

00:21:29.960 --> 00:21:34.080
Did I miss something, though, about, like, the memo on being able to jump higher?

00:21:34.100 --> 00:21:40.940
Or is it just during this particular part of the boss fight where all of a sudden your character jumps a little higher so that he can reach the head?

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:43.700
No, I think you just jump higher by using B.

00:21:43.920 --> 00:21:46.640
If you use B and A at any time when you're standing still...

00:21:47.600 --> 00:21:49.480
Maybe that wasn't. I think it's when you...

00:21:49.960 --> 00:21:54.420
When you press a directional button and jump, that's when you jump high.

00:21:54.720 --> 00:22:02.420
But also, I could be wrong, but I'm pretty sure if you were just holding B as if you're running and then press A, you jump high, even if you're standing still.

00:22:02.760 --> 00:22:03.700
Huh. Okay.

00:22:04.040 --> 00:22:08.040
Both of those things check out because maybe because it's a limited space that you're in with the boss.

00:22:08.220 --> 00:22:12.340
I was just trying to use just the A button and the directions.

00:22:12.520 --> 00:22:16.100
But what it turned out was that what I had to do was...

00:22:16.100 --> 00:22:17.120
And this is just in my own head.

00:22:17.120 --> 00:22:18.940
I'm not saying the manuals that do this.

00:22:19.200 --> 00:22:29.880
Is that I'd have to kind of run, jump, and then use the left pad and then switch to the right pad immediately to jump up high.

00:22:30.060 --> 00:22:31.440
And then I could throw the hammer.

00:22:31.860 --> 00:22:35.420
And that just felt like I was like, all right, nobody ever trained you for this morning.

00:22:36.200 --> 00:22:41.420
And so I was throwing hammers at the first boss for an awful long time thinking like, does he just take a lot of hits?

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:43.080
Like, why isn't he throwing anything at me?

00:22:43.260 --> 00:22:44.840
And then it's like, no, you need to hit the head.

00:22:54.840 --> 00:22:56.240
Right.

00:22:56.260 --> 00:22:57.140
Yeah.

00:22:57.620 --> 00:23:06.840
But yeah, to your point, there's no point in the game where you notice like when you hit anything before these bosses that they like glow as if you've hit them, that they give you that kind of feedback.

00:23:07.240 --> 00:23:09.800
And now that's the only feedback that this boss's head gives you.

00:23:09.920 --> 00:23:14.660
So like if you're hitting its body, you don't know to look for feedback because nothing else has given you that.

00:23:14.660 --> 00:23:18.120
There are some enemies that will change color though when they require two hits.

00:23:18.480 --> 00:23:19.760
Yeah. But that's still not the same thing.

00:23:19.760 --> 00:23:20.780
No, no, I know. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:23:20.920 --> 00:23:25.900
Just like sometimes color has been indicative of like, you know, oh, that means you have to do something.

00:23:26.120 --> 00:23:27.260
Right. Oh, yeah.

00:23:27.260 --> 00:23:30.780
Or those things that run up behind you and they turn blue and freeze for a second.

00:23:30.980 --> 00:23:33.220
What the heck are those? Actually, I have the manual right here.

00:23:34.060 --> 00:23:35.000
All the names.

00:23:35.260 --> 00:23:36.460
They're coyotes. Okay.

00:23:36.560 --> 00:23:41.900
Yeah. But the names of the rest of the enemies are literally just keyboard mashes.

00:23:42.460 --> 00:23:43.680
What? You don't think pooter?

00:23:44.320 --> 00:23:45.640
What is that supposed to be?

00:23:45.720 --> 00:23:47.420
It's a pig. A pooter is a pig?

00:23:47.560 --> 00:23:49.380
Okay. Sneal? The snail?

00:23:49.820 --> 00:23:50.940
Sneal the snail.

00:23:51.320 --> 00:23:52.800
Snail is probably...

00:23:52.800 --> 00:23:57.900
Sneal and coyote are the only ones that bear any resemblance to what they're supposed to be.

00:23:58.320 --> 00:23:59.740
Cobra? Okay.

00:23:59.820 --> 00:24:01.340
Sorry. Cobra. Three.

00:24:01.460 --> 00:24:02.800
One that doesn't resemble.

00:24:03.120 --> 00:24:04.760
That's it. Yeah.

00:24:05.460 --> 00:24:07.760
Whaler isn't really like a swordfish.

00:24:09.240 --> 00:24:10.820
Red oct and blue oct.

00:24:11.020 --> 00:24:15.820
Check out though. Stop picking apart my hyperbole.

00:24:15.820 --> 00:24:21.880
I'm sure you could take any sentence I've ever said on nostalgia and just rip it to shreds if you just tried hard enough.

00:24:22.720 --> 00:24:26.400
The one thing though on these bosses and the reason why we're spending so much time on them is because...

00:24:27.660 --> 00:24:37.160
So you defeat the first boss and was I the only one thinking like, okay, whatever, he grew another head and he goes up to the next stage and now you've got to take care of him.

00:24:37.820 --> 00:24:39.800
Then you go and do the same fight again?

00:24:40.100 --> 00:24:41.200
It's the same.

00:24:41.440 --> 00:24:43.520
Yeah, it's exactly the same. It's not even more difficult.

00:24:43.760 --> 00:24:45.500
It's not even like he takes more hits to die or anything.

00:24:45.500 --> 00:24:46.640
It does take more hits. Oh, he does.

00:24:46.720 --> 00:24:48.760
Yeah, but it's ever slightly increasing.

00:24:49.000 --> 00:24:50.220
Gotcha. They are supposedly.

00:24:50.500 --> 00:24:51.600
They're not the same guy though.

00:24:51.860 --> 00:24:53.700
They're different characters technically.

00:24:53.740 --> 00:24:56.320
I thought they were the same guy and he changes the head.

00:24:56.820 --> 00:24:58.980
He just changes his head like in his wardrobe?

00:24:59.180 --> 00:25:03.580
He just changes his head, yeah. Yeah. He never like falls through the pit, does he?

00:25:03.880 --> 00:25:06.280
No, no, no. But he does blow up.

00:25:06.480 --> 00:25:07.440
Okay. Got it.

00:25:07.520 --> 00:25:11.060
Yeah. So it's more like Bowser being like, I was really a Goomba.

00:25:11.580 --> 00:25:12.860
Yeah, exactly. Yeah, okay.

00:25:13.980 --> 00:25:22.120
Yeah, the difference is though is that in Super Mario Brothers, even though you always fought Bowser at the end of each world, he got more complicated each time.

00:25:22.220 --> 00:25:33.800
Yeah. Where he would do like, oh, now there's this platform that you have to like try to jump over or now you have to come in on something where you must, you can't jump over right away.

00:25:33.980 --> 00:25:36.160
You have to go under and then jump over Bowser.

00:25:36.360 --> 00:25:38.180
There was like a, there was a thing to it.

00:25:38.460 --> 00:25:41.740
Here, he doesn't gain like any new powers.

00:25:41.740 --> 00:25:47.700
He doesn't like throw hammers at you as well or anything or do or stomp to like paralyze you.

00:25:47.920 --> 00:25:51.900
It's just, hey, here's that like slow ball, fireball thing I got again.

00:25:52.080 --> 00:25:56.360
You want some of that? But that's my problem with the levels themselves as well.

00:25:56.560 --> 00:26:01.020
Like, yeah, like this is sort of going into what you mentioned about it sort of being zoomed in.

00:26:02.060 --> 00:26:07.600
And to me, these are just very basic designs.

00:26:07.600 --> 00:26:15.220
Like, it's too basic of a design for it to be that interesting because you're running forward and you're jumping when you need to jump.

00:26:15.700 --> 00:26:25.140
And the, yes, there are enemies in places that like it's intuitive to hit them, but I don't see it as all that creative.

00:26:25.520 --> 00:26:27.520
There's no real sense of progress either.

00:26:27.520 --> 00:26:28.500
No. Going along.

00:26:28.800 --> 00:26:31.180
I don't really feel like I'm getting closer to an end.

00:26:31.460 --> 00:26:38.340
No. And maybe that's just because of the four stages, eight worlds, four checkpoints in each stage.

00:26:38.700 --> 00:26:40.560
What did you guys think of those like little checkpoints?

00:26:40.560 --> 00:26:42.520
I didn't understand the reason they were there.

00:26:42.560 --> 00:26:43.460
I liked them actually.

00:26:43.480 --> 00:26:47.500
I thought that it was, I mean, when you die, you go back to that checkpoint.

00:26:47.840 --> 00:26:51.100
Yeah. So I thought that was a nice little, it made the levels feel really long.

00:26:51.100 --> 00:26:52.000
I guess that makes more sense.

00:26:52.000 --> 00:26:59.260
And then also like the levels felt really long because there wasn't like a moment, nothing happened when you get reached a checkpoint.

00:26:59.440 --> 00:27:01.900
You just keep going. So it doesn't, there's not like a break.

00:27:02.000 --> 00:27:09.140
I guess the only reason that I would know that I was any further in these levels is that the checkpoint number changed because there's no variety of layout.

00:27:09.400 --> 00:27:11.440
Yeah. The layout repeats itself constantly.

00:27:11.600 --> 00:27:13.600
And you need those goal markers actually.

00:27:13.660 --> 00:27:19.440
All the platforms are, I feel like all the platforms are cut to the same size.

00:27:19.440 --> 00:27:26.740
Like it's always this like one eighth of the screen taken up by a platform and then you jump to the next one.

00:27:26.800 --> 00:27:28.440
That's the exact, that looks exactly the same.

00:27:29.140 --> 00:27:32.660
So I was, I was not smitten by the level design.

00:27:33.100 --> 00:27:41.920
Yeah. And there's actually, there's more things that Super Mario Brothers has in terms of platforming layouts than Adventure Island has.

00:27:42.040 --> 00:27:45.640
And meanwhile, this game comes out four years later.

00:27:45.800 --> 00:27:47.160
Yeah. You know, three years later.

00:27:47.160 --> 00:27:57.320
So it's like, that's a little strange that they managed to copy a lot of things that it had, but that they couldn't fit in all of it or rather even think of newer solves for platforming.

00:27:57.400 --> 00:28:07.480
Yeah. You know, it's almost like this game needed either a different kind of a variety of enemies at some point introduced into the game,

00:28:07.480 --> 00:28:15.040
or it needed a like a new jumping feature where you could maybe like double jump with a certain power up.

00:28:15.260 --> 00:28:21.540
But instead they went the wrong way with the platforming power ups and they give you that skateboard.

00:28:22.000 --> 00:28:24.100
Yeah. It makes you worse at things.

00:28:24.560 --> 00:28:31.780
Basically the only good it gives you is, yeah, you're a little faster and you technically have an extra hit.

00:28:31.780 --> 00:28:35.460
I think of it, I only thought of the skateboard strictly from an armor perspective.

00:28:35.600 --> 00:28:38.780
Yeah. All I cared about was like, oh, well, I can get a little bit further before I lose it.

00:28:38.800 --> 00:28:49.080
I actually didn't hate the skateboard because I thought it was intentionally like a plus in that if you get hit, it's an extra hit that you get to take.

00:28:49.200 --> 00:28:53.860
But then intentionally also a minus that you can't stop moving, which makes it harder.

00:28:53.860 --> 00:29:02.080
I thought it was kind of a cool little like take on, like instead of giving you a star, which they have their equivalent of the star in this game anyways,

00:29:02.180 --> 00:29:06.640
but they give you something that like, oh, this boosts you up, but it's going to be harder to keep because you have to keep moving.

00:29:06.760 --> 00:29:09.440
I thought that was kind of a cool little fun aside.

00:29:09.700 --> 00:29:13.400
I just didn't enjoy being on the skateboard, so I count it as a negative.

00:29:13.800 --> 00:29:19.240
I also just think that the idea of constantly moving forward because you can't stop the skateboard.

00:29:19.240 --> 00:29:22.480
Yeah, you can't adjust your platforming if you fall into a hole.

00:29:22.480 --> 00:29:27.780
There just comes a point where, you know, depending on which levels you get the skateboard in,

00:29:27.960 --> 00:29:32.280
you're bound to like maybe get like two or three jumps over something before you lose it again

00:29:32.280 --> 00:29:37.660
because it's just the screen is just littered with like sort of perfect jumps required to keep that skateboard going

00:29:37.660 --> 00:29:45.260
because you can stop when you're yourself, you know, like you can kind of land perfectly without like skidding too much

00:29:45.260 --> 00:29:47.120
and take care of the next enemy.

00:29:47.320 --> 00:29:51.900
But on the skateboard, you're forced to continue moving forward and it's like, I just don't have that kind of movement.

00:29:51.900 --> 00:29:57.600
And that's where there's that little bit of like risk reward you have to do in your head real quick of like,

00:29:58.100 --> 00:30:01.760
is the next section going to be hard enough where I might as well have the skateboard?

00:30:01.920 --> 00:30:08.560
You don't always get that time to deliberate though because the way that these eggs sort of spawn is that

00:30:08.560 --> 00:30:13.600
if you're just running through them, they will pop and fall right next to you.

00:30:13.700 --> 00:30:15.600
You just have to pick it up.

00:30:15.600 --> 00:30:18.400
I barely ever saw anything come out of an egg before I just had it.

00:30:18.780 --> 00:30:24.860
You know, like. See, I felt like I usually was able to see the egg ahead of time, shoot it, open it and see what it was.

00:30:25.040 --> 00:30:26.000
You would crack the eggs.

00:30:26.120 --> 00:30:29.420
I cracked the eggs until I started to notice the eggplant thing, which is another thing.

00:30:29.420 --> 00:30:35.840
You can. It's just if you're trying to like, if you're in a flow, you're not just going to slow down and have to speed up again.

00:30:35.840 --> 00:30:45.180
So I just would run through it and hope it was a honey girl and I'd be invincible.

00:30:45.660 --> 00:30:47.740
Sean, just clarify for everyone listening at home.

00:30:47.820 --> 00:30:49.860
What's a honey girl? It's like your own turn.

00:30:50.520 --> 00:30:52.360
Yeah, you know, like a little, you know.

